      "id": "2058220599583920153",
      "text": "The Starship V3 heat shield held well",
      "created_at": "Sat May 23 16:16:45 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": null,
      "quoted": {
        "id": "2058165850134204554",
        "text": "We need heat shields to protect us, since we use the air to slow us down as we return to Earth. \nFrom orbital speed, it gets to 1650°C / 3000°F. From the Moon: 2750°C / 5000°F. \nFor yesterday's Starship suborbital test flight, peak was 1450°C / 2600°F. Great to see the @SpaceX progress over the last 3 flights. Making them truly reusable is complex and necessary for permanent, cheap space access. \nimage compilation: @niccruzpatane",
